{"name": "TAI - Explain Predictions with Shapley", "creationTimeStamp": null, "modifiedTimeStamp": null, "createdBy": null, "modifiedBy": null, "displayName": null, "localDisplayName": null, "properties": null, "links": null, "metadataVersion": null, "version": null, "type": "code", "flowMetadata": null, "ui": "{\"showPageContentOnly\": true, \"pages\": [{\"id\": \"designPage\", \"type\": \"page\", \"label\": \"Design\", \"children\": [{\"id\": \"refData\", \"type\": \"inputtable\", \"label\": \"Select Reference Data Table (Background Dataset):\", \"required\": true, \"placeholder\": \"Select background dataset for reference\"}, {\"id\": \"targetVar\", \"type\": \"columnselector\", \"label\": \"Specify Predicted Target Column:\", \"table\": \"refData\", \"max\": 1, \"min\": 1, \"required\": true, \"columntype\": \"n\", \"include\": null}, {\"id\": \"intervalVars\", \"type\": \"columnselector\", \"label\": \"Specify Interval Inputs:\", \"table\": \"refData\", \"multiple\": true, \"required\": false, \"columntype\": \"n\", \"include\": null}, {\"id\": \"nominalVars\", \"type\": \"columnselector\", \"label\": \"Specify Nominal Inputs:\", \"table\": \"refData\", \"multiple\": true, \"required\": false, \"include\": null}]}, {\"id\": \"configPage\", \"type\": \"page\", \"label\": \"Configuration\", \"children\": [{\"id\": \"astoreTable\", \"type\": \"inputtable\", \"label\": \"Analytic Store Model Table\", \"required\": false, \"placeholder\": \"Select an ASTORE model table\"}, {\"id\": \"weightVar\", \"type\": \"columnselector\", \"label\": \"Select a weight column:\", \"table\": \"refData\", \"max\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"required\": false, \"columntype\": \"n\", \"include\": null}, {\"id\": \"methodType\", \"type\": \"dropdown\", \"label\": \"Explanation Method:\", \"items\": [{\"value\": \"HYPERSHAP\", \"label\": \"HyperSHAP\"}, {\"value\": \"KERNELSHAP\", \"label\": \"KernelSHAP\"}], \"required\": true}, {\"id\": \"hyperOptionsSec\", \"type\": \"section\", \"label\": \"HyperSHAP Method Options\", \"visible\": [\"$methodType\", \"=\", \"HYPERSHAP\"], \"open\": true, \"children\": [{\"id\": \"hyperDepth\", \"type\": \"numstepper\", \"label\": \"Maximum Depth of Coalitional Approximation:\", \"required\": true, \"integer\": true, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 2}]}, {\"id\": \"kernelOptionsSec\", \"type\": \"section\", \"label\": \"KernelSHAP Method Options\", \"visible\": [\"$methodType\", \"=\", \"KERNELSHAP\"], \"open\": true, \"children\": [{\"id\": \"kernelBinWidth\", \"type\": \"numstepper\", \"label\": \"Bin Width for Interval Variables:\", \"required\": true, \"decimalPlaces\": 4, \"min\": 0}, {\"id\": \"kernelIncMissing\", \"type\": \"checkbox\", \"label\": \"Include missing values in calculations\"}, {\"id\": \"kernelSampleSize\", \"type\": \"numstepper\", \"label\": \"Sample Size (Number of coalition samples):\", \"required\": true, \"integer\": true, \"min\": 1}, {\"id\": \"kernelSeed\", \"type\": \"numstepper\", \"label\": \"Random Seed:\", \"required\": false, \"integer\": true, \"min\": 0}, {\"id\": \"kernelUseRaw\", \"type\": \"checkbox\", \"label\": \"Use raw data for calculation\"}]}]}, {\"id\": \"aboutPage\", \"type\": \"page\", \"label\": \"About\", \"children\": [{\"id\": \"aboutText\", \"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"TAI - Explain Predictions with Shapley\\n\\nThis custom step executes PROC SHAPLEY in SAS to compute Shapley values for explaining machine learning model predictions. the step examines your predictive model and shows how each input variable contributed to the model's predictions. This can help you understand which factors were most important and build confidence in the model's results.\\n\\nMethods Supported:\\n     HyperSHAP: Fast approximation method optimized for tree-based models.\\n     KernelSHAP: Model-agnostic kernel-based approximation method for general models.\\n\\nThe step can help you:\\n     See which variables have the biggest impact on predictions.\\n     Understand the factors driving model decisions.\\n     Explain model results to business users, managers, auditors, or other stakeholders.\\n     Improve transparency when working with machine learning models.\\n\\nBy making model predictions easier to understand, this step helps users move beyond what the model predicted and better understand why it made that prediction.\\n\\nUse the Design tab to supply input datasets and configure model roles. Adjust algorithm-specific hyperparameters under the Configuration tab.\\n\\nMore information about PROC SHAPLEY:\\nhttps://go.documentation.sas.com/doc/cn/pgmsascdc/v_072/casml/casml_shapley_toc.htm\"}, {\"id\": \"contact_section\", \"type\": \"section\", \"label\": \"Created / contact\", \"open\": true, \"visible\": \"\", \"children\": [{\"id\": \"created_contact_text\", \"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Dawn Pancholi (Shubham.Pancholi@sas.com)\", \"visible\": \"\"}]}, {\"id\": \"version_section\", \"type\": \"section\", \"label\": \"Version\", \"open\": true, \"visible\": \"\", \"children\": [{\"id\": \"version_text\", \"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Version : 1.0.3 (28JUL2026)\"}]}]}], \"syntaxversion\": \"1.3.0\", \"values\": {\"refData\": {\"library\": \"\", \"table\": \"\"}, \"targetVar\": [], \"intervalVars\": [], \"nominalVars\": [], \"astoreTable\": {\"library\": \"\", \"table\": \"\"}, \"weightVar\": [], \"methodType\": \"HYPERSHAP\", \"hyperDepth\": 1, \"kernelBinWidth\": 0.1, \"kernelIncMissing\": false, \"kernelSampleSize\": 500, \"kernelSeed\": null, \"kernelUseRaw\": false}, \"promptHierarchies\": []}", "templates": {"SAS": "/************************************************************************\nTrustworthy AI (TAI) - Explain Predictions with Shapley\n\nPurpose: This SAS program executes PROC SHAPLEY to compute Shapley values \nfor explaining machine learning model predictions. It supports both \nHyperSHAP and KernelSHAP methods with method-specific parameter controls.\n\nInput Parameters:\n- refData: Reference data table containing background observations (macro variable)\n- intervalVars: List of interval input variables (macro variable)\n- nominalVars: List of nominal input variables (macro variable)\n- targetVar: Predicted target variable containing model predictions (macro variable)\n- weightVar: Optional weight variable (macro variable)\n- astoreTable: Optional Analytic Store (ASTORE) table (macro variable)\n- methodType: Explainer method, HYPERSHAP or KERNELSHAP (macro variable)\n\nMethod - HyperSHAP Options:\n- hyperDepth: Maximum depth of coalitional approximation (Default: 1)\n\nMethod - KernelSHAP Options:\n- kernelBinWidth: Bin width for interval variables (Default: 0.1)\n- kernelIncMissing: Flag to include missing values (1=Yes, 0=No)\n- kernelSampleSize: Number of coalition samples to generate (Default: 500)\n- kernelSeed: Random seed value for KernelSHAP method (macro variable)\n- kernelUseRaw: Flag to specify whether to use raw data (1=Yes, 0=No)\n\n\nTested in SAS Viya 2026.05\nVersion: 1.0.3 (28JUL2026)\n************************************************************************/;\n\n\n/************************************************************************\nMACRO DEFINITION\n************************************************************************/;\n\n\n/* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------* \n   Macro to set up the error flagging and determine how Proc Shapley should run assuming all required fields\n   Have been filled out\n   If there's a major component missing (specified in the if statement) then the if block will execute and throw an error\n   Otherwise, the else block containing the proc shapley will execute\n*------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ */\n%macro _shapley;\n\n    /* Ensure required parameters are provided before executing */\n    %if %sysevalf(%superq(refData)=, boolean) or \n        %sysevalf(%superq(targetVar)=, boolean) or\n        (\n            %sysevalf(%superq(intervalVars)=, boolean) and\n            %sysevalf(%superq(nominalVars)=, boolean)\n        ) %then %do;\n        %put ERROR: Missing required parameters. Please check your SAS Studio Flow inputs and Target Variable selection.;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        \n        /* If astoreTable has no value in the UI then make sure it's set equal to nothing so that it doesn't throw a warning */\n        %if not %symexist(astoreTable) %then %let astoreTable=;\n        \n        /* Create the data for Proc Shapley that only needs one row of the reference data */\n        data CASUSER._QUERY;\n            set &refData(obs=1);\n        run; \n        \n        /* Execute the Trustworthy AI PROC SHAPLEY step */\n        proc shapley data=CASUSER._QUERY referencedata=&refData;\n            \n            /* Reference an Analytic Store (ASTORE) model if provided */\n            %if %sysevalf(%superq(astoreTable)=, boolean) = 0 %then %do;\n                astoremodel rstore=&astoreTable.;\n            %end;\n\n            /* Define Interval input variables if specified */\n            %if %sysevalf(%superq(intervalVars)=, boolean) = 0 %then %do;\n                input &intervalVars. / level=interval;\n            %end;\n\n            /* Define Nominal input variables if specified */\n            %if %sysevalf(%superq(nominalVars)=, boolean) = 0 %then %do;\n                input &nominalVars. / level=nominal;\n            %end;\n\n            /* Specify the Predicted Target Column */\n            predictedtarget &targetVar.;\n\n            /* Set observational weight if specified */\n            %if %sysevalf(%superq(weightVar)=, boolean) = 0 %then %do;\n                weight &weightVar.;\n            %end;\n\n            /* Construct dynamic METHOD statement based on selection */\n            %if %upcase(&methodType.) = HYPERSHAP %then %do;\n                method hypershap (\n                    /*%if %sysevalf(%superq(hyperSeed)=, boolean) = 0 %then seed=&hyperSeed. ;*/\n                    /*%if &hyperUseRaw. = 1 %then useRawData ;*/\n                    %if %sysevalf(%superq(hyperDepth)=, boolean) = 0 %then depth=&hyperDepth. ;\n                );\n            %end;\n            %else %if %upcase(&methodType.) = KERNELSHAP %then %do;\n                method kernelshap (\n                    %if %sysevalf(%superq(kernelBinWidth)=, boolean) = 0 %then binwidth=&kernelBinWidth. ;\n                    %if &kernelIncMissing. = 1 %then includeMissing ;\n                    %if %sysevalf(%superq(kernelSampleSize)=, boolean) = 0 %then sampleSize=&kernelSampleSize. ;\n                    %if %sysevalf(%superq(kernelSeed)=, boolean) = 0 %then seed=&kernelSeed. ;\n                    %if &kernelUseRaw. = 1 %then useRawData ;\n                );\n            %end;\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _shapley;\n\n/************************************************************************\nEXECUTION CODE\n************************************************************************/;\n\nTITLE1 \"Shapley\";\n\n%_shapley;\n\ntitle;\nfootnote;\n\n%sysmacdelete _shapley; "}}